<%- include('partials/head-assets') %>
</head>
<body>

<%- include('partials/nav') %>

<main id="main">
<article class="post">
  <div class="meta">Last updated: 11 October 2026</div>
  <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
  <p>ColoringPageMaker needs no account and uses no cookies, analytics or advertising. This page lists the data the site handles, where it goes and why.</p>

  <h2>Who runs this site</h2>
  <p>ColoringPageMaker (www.coloringpagemaker.app) is run by Peak Apps Studio. For any question about your data, email <a href="mailto:info@peakappsstudio.com">info@peakappsstudio.com</a>.</p>

  <h2>When you make a page</h2>
  <p>When you press generate, your browser sends your description and the detail level you chose to our server. The server adds its own drawing instructions and sends the text to OpenAI's image service, which draws the page. The image comes back to your browser. We do not save your descriptions or your images.</p>
  <p>Your descriptions go to OpenAI, so please do not include a child's name or other personal details in them. Under OpenAI's API data policy, data sent through the API is kept for up to 30 days to monitor abuse and, by default, is not used to train OpenAI's models.</p>

  <h2>Daily limits and your IP address</h2>
  <p>Free pages are limited to two a day. To count them, the server stores a counter under your IP address in our database (Upstash Redis, connected through Vercel). Each counter is deleted automatically after 24 hours. For Pro, the daily counter is stored under your Pro email address instead and is deleted after 24 hours in the same way.</p>

  <h2>PDF downloads</h2>
  <p>On the home page, the PDF is built in your browser, and the PDF library loads from cdnjs, a public code library run by Cloudflare. On the theme pages, your browser sends the pages you made to our server, which builds the PDF in memory, sends it back and does not keep a copy.</p>

  <h2>What is stored in your browser</h2>
  <ul class="post-list-items">
    <li>The pages you made in this visit are kept in your browser's session storage so they survive a page reload. They are deleted when you close the tab.</li>
    <li>If you activate Pro, your Pro email address is saved in your browser's local storage so that Pro stays on. To remove it, press the "Pro active" button on the home page and confirm "Sign out of Pro on this device", or clear this site's data.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Pro and your email address</h2>
  <p>Pro is sold through Gumroad. The buy buttons open Gumroad's checkout, where you give your payment details to Gumroad, not to us. When Gumroad notifies our server of a sale, or when you activate Pro with your license key, the server checks the key with Gumroad's license service (api.gumroad.com). It then stores your purchase email address with the Gumroad sale ID and the date Pro was granted, so it can recognise you as a Pro user. If you activate with your email address instead of a key, the server looks that address up in the same records. Your Pro email is also sent with each page you generate or download, so the server can apply the Pro limits. This record stays until a refund is reported to us or you ask us to delete it. As the seller, we also see your email address and order details in Gumroad, and we use them to answer questions and issue refunds.</p>

  <h2>Hosting and fonts</h2>
  <p>The site runs on Vercel. Like any web host, Vercel processes each request, including your IP address, the page you asked for and your browser type, and keeps request logs for a limited time. If something fails, our server writes a technical error message to those logs. The fonts are served from this site, so no font service sees your visit.</p>

  <h2>Emails</h2>
  <p>If you email us, we receive your email address and your message. Mail sent to peakappsstudio.com addresses is forwarded by Forward Email to a Gmail inbox. We use your email only to reply to you.</p>

  <h2>Who else receives data</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="data-table">
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Company</th><th scope="col">What for</th><th scope="col">Privacy policy</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row">OpenAI</th><td>Drawing your coloring pages from your descriptions</td><td><a href="https://openai.com/policies/privacy-policy/" rel="noopener">openai.com</a></td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Vercel</th><td>Hosting the site and its server</td><td><a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-notice" rel="noopener">vercel.com</a></td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Upstash</th><td>The database for daily counters and Pro records</td><td><a href="https://upstash.com/trust/privacy.pdf" rel="noopener">upstash.com</a></td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Gumroad</th><td>Checkout, payments and license checks</td><td><a href="https://gumroad.com/privacy" rel="noopener">gumroad.com</a></td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Cloudflare</th><td>Serving the PDF library on the home page (cdnjs)</td><td><a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener">cloudflare.com</a></td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Google</th><td>The Gmail inbox for our email</td><td><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">policies.google.com</a></td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Forward Email</th><td>Forwarding mail sent to our address</td><td><a href="https://forwardemail.net/en/privacy" rel="noopener">forwardemail.net</a></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>Most of these companies are based in the United States, so your data may be processed there. We do not sell your data, and we do not share it with advertisers.</p>

  <h2>How long data is kept</h2>
  <ul class="post-list-items">
    <li>Descriptions and images: not kept by us. Requests to OpenAI: up to 30 days, under OpenAI's API data policy.</li>
    <li>Daily counters under your IP address or Pro email: 24 hours.</li>
    <li>Pro records (email, Gumroad sale ID, date): until a refund is reported or you ask us to delete them.</li>
    <li>Pages in your browser: until you close the tab. Your Pro email in your browser: until you sign out or clear this site's data.</li>
    <li>Hosting logs: kept by Vercel for a limited time under its own policy. Purchase records: kept by Gumroad under its own policy.</li>
    <li>Emails to us: until we delete them. Ask us and we will delete yours, unless we need it as a record of a payment or refund.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>You can ask us for a copy of the personal data we hold about you, ask us to correct or delete it, or object to how we use it. Email <a href="mailto:info@peakappsstudio.com">info@peakappsstudio.com</a> and we will reply within one month. If you live in the EU or the UK, you can also complain to your local data protection authority.</p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>ColoringPageMaker is made for adults: parents, teachers and sellers who make coloring pages, often for children to color. The free tier asks for no name, email address or account. The site is not meant to be used by children on their own, and we do not knowingly collect personal data from children under 13. If you think a child has given us personal data, for example an email address in the Pro form, email us and we will delete it.</p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>If the site starts handling data differently, we will update this page and the date at the top.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Peak Apps Studio, <a href="mailto:info@peakappsstudio.com">info@peakappsstudio.com</a>. See also our <a href="/terms">terms of use</a>.</p>
</article>
</main>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
</body>
</html>
